---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const title = "Alexios Loukis — Cloud & DevOps";
const description =
  "Final-year Information Systems student in Patras, Greece, moving into cloud and DevOps engineering. Docker, Linux, CI/CD, and Azure.";
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <main>
    <h1>Alexios Loukis</h1>
    <p class="tagline">Cloud &amp; DevOps · Patras, Greece</p>

    <p class="lede">
      I build and automate infrastructure. Right now that means containers,
      Linux and CI/CD pipelines, and learning Azure and Terraform properly
      rather than quickly. Final-year Information Systems student at the
      University of Patras, graduating June 2027 and looking for a junior cloud
      or DevOps role.
    </p>

    <section>
      <h2>Current state</h2>

      <div class="status">
        <div class="status-row">
          <span class="tag tag-live">running</span>
          <span class="stack">
            Docker · Docker Compose · Linux · Bash · Python · Git · GitHub
            Actions
          </span>
        </div>

        <div class="status-row">
          <span class="tag tag-progress">applying</span>
          <span class="stack">
            Microsoft Azure · Terraform
            <span class="note">AZ-104 Azure Administrator — expected Oct 2026</span>
          </span>
        </div>

        <div class="status-row">
          <span class="tag tag-queued">queued</span>
          <span class="stack">
            Kubernetes · Observability (Prometheus, Grafana) · Cloud security
          </span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Projects</h2>

      <div class="entry">
        <div class="entry-head">
          <h3>Multi-container web app with Redis caching</h3>
          <span class="tag tag-live">shipped</span>
        </div>
        <p class="entry-tech">
          Docker · Docker Compose · Python/Flask · Redis · GitHub Actions
        </p>
        <p>
          A two-tier web API — Flask application backed by Redis as an in-memory
          store — orchestrated with Docker Compose. Built on an Alpine base
          image to keep size and attack surface small, with a GitHub Actions
          pipeline that builds and tests the image on every push so a broken
          build never reaches main.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="https://github.com/AlexiosLoukis/flask-redis-docker-compose"
            >Source on GitHub →</a
          >
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="entry">
        <div class="entry-head">
          <h3>Azure infrastructure as code</h3>
          <span class="tag tag-progress">in progress</span>
        </div>
        <p class="entry-tech">Terraform · Microsoft Azure · GitHub Actions</p>
        <p>
          Provisioning a complete Azure environment from code — resource group,
          virtual network with segmented subnets, network security groups, a
          virtual machine and Key Vault — with Terraform state held remotely in
          an Azure Storage Account so changes are safe to make repeatedly.
        </p>
        <p>
          The pipeline runs <code>plan</code> on every pull request and
          <code>apply</code> on merge, authenticating to Azure through OIDC
          federation instead of a stored secret.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Background</h2>

      <div class="record">
        <span class="when">2023 — 2027</span>
        <div>
          <strong>BSc Management Science &amp; Technology</strong>
          <p class="where">
            University of Patras · Information Systems track
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="record">
        <span class="when">2023</span>
        <div>
          <strong>IT Support &amp; Hardware Technician</strong>
          <p class="where">
            Erasmus+ placement · Universal Mobility SL · Valencia, Spain
          </p>
          <p>
            Front-line technical support across two repair centres — diagnosing
            OS, software and hardware faults for walk-in clients, and handling
            installations and migrations across macOS, Windows and Linux.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="record">
        <span class="when">2021</span>
        <div>
          <strong>Junior Hardware Technician</strong>
          <p class="where">
            Erasmus+ placement · ITEK Informática · Braga, Portugal
          </p>
          <p>
            Selected at 16 for a European vocational training placement abroad.
            Customer technical support, hardware diagnostics and software
            configuration in an IT retail environment.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Where this is going</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        Cloud engineering first, then security. You cannot secure infrastructure
        you do not know how to build — so I am learning to build it properly
        before I try to defend it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <ul class="links">
        <li><a href="https://github.com/AlexiosLoukis">GitHub</a></li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/alexiosloukis/">LinkedIn</a>
        </li>
        <li><a href="mailto:loykhsalexhs@gmail.com">Email</a></li>
        <li><a href="/cv.pdf">CV (PDF)</a></li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <footer>Built with Astro. Deployed from GitHub.</footer>
  </main>
</Base>